Consumer Health Privacy Notice - Telix Pharmaceuticals

Home Consumer Health Privacy Notice Consumer Health Privacy Notice

Consumer Health Privacy Notice

This Consumer Health Privacy Notice (“Notice”) applies to all operations for Telix Pharmaceuticals (US) Inc (“Telix US” or “we”) and supplements the Global Privacy Policy for Telix Pharmaceuticals Limited. It applies solely to health information or health data as defined by Washington and Nevada law (“Consumer Health Information”) to provide additional information about how Telix may process Consumer Health Information, how we protect it, as well as your rights and choices with respect to that information. It applies to all operations for Telix US, as well as its websites, mobile applications, and digital services (“Services”) that link to or post this Notice.

This Notice applies only to residents of Washington and Nevada and to individuals whose information is processed in Washington or Nevada. It does not apply to the personal information we process about Telix workforce members, third party partners, or personal information that is governed by other applicable laws, including protected health information we may process as a business associate under the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (“HIPAA”) of 1996.

Consumer Health Information for purposes of this Notice is defined by Washington or Nevada law and includes information that identifies or is reasonably capable of being associated or linked, directly or indirectly, with a particular consumer and that identifies the consumer’s past, present, or future physical or mental health status.

1. Categories of Consumer Health Information Collected

Telix US may collect and process the following categories of Consumer Health Information:

Individual health conditions, treatment, diseases, or diagnoses;

Social, psychological, behavioral, and medical interventions;

Health-related surgeries or procedures;

Use or purchase of prescribed medication or ordered product;

Bodily functions, vital signs, symptoms, or measurements of health information;

Diagnoses or diagnostic testing, treatment, or medication;

Genetic data;

Precise location information that could reasonably indicate a resident’s attempt to acquire or receive health services or supplies;

Data that identifies a consumer seeking health care services; and

Consumer health information inferred or derived from non-health information.

2. Sources From Which Consumer Health Information May Be Collected:

Telix US may collect Consumer Health Information directly from:

You, your mobile devices and your computer and other internet-connected devices upon downloading and when you visit or interact with our physical sites, websites, applications, and online platforms;

Third parties including joint marketing and advertising partners who provide digital marketing services, website and other digital, marketing or online security services;

Publicly available sources including public databases, government sources and other third parties;

Other Telix entities;

Third parties and processors who provide benefit verification, program, enrollment, and product fulfillment services in connection with our products and services;

Third parties and processors who help us maintain the accuracy of our data and data aggregators that help us complete and enhance our records;

Third parties and processors that provide access to information you make publicly available, such as social media platforms; and

Third parties and processors who assist with fraud prevention, detection, and mitigation.

3. Purposes for Processing Consumer Health Information

Telix US may process the above-mentioned categories of Consumer Health Information for the following purposes:

To provide, maintain, and improve our products and services;

To process transactions and fulfill requests initiated by you;

To communicate with you and provide you support, such as to address your inquiries and other communications you send to us;

To operate, evaluate, and improve our business, such as sending you information about our services, performing accounting, auditing, record keeping, and other internal functions, conducting research, developing new products and services, analyzing and improving our sites and services, personalizing your experience, and implementing various business development matters (e.g., mergers, acquisitions, and other business transactions);

To comply with applicable legal, regulatory and contractual obligations;

To detect, prevent, and respond to security incidents or fraudulent activity; and

To verify or maintain the quality or safety of a product, service, or device that is owned, manufactured by, manufactured for, or controlled by us, and to improve, upgrade, or enhance the service or device that is owned, manufactured, manufactured for, or controlled by us.

4. Sharing of Consumer Health Information

We may share each of the above categories of Consumer Health Information with third parties and affiliates such as:

Other Telix Pharmaceutical Limited entities;

Third-party services providers who perform services on our behalf including third-parties:

that help administer, manage, and analyze our programs and services;

with whom we have joint marketing and similar arrangements or who assist with our information technology and security programs;

who provide marketing and data analytics services, such as social media platforms used to deliver our ads, website/email optimization providers, email marketing vendors, and data analytics vendors;

who are network advertising partners;

who assist with fraud prevention, detection, and mitigation;

who are reasonably necessary to facilitate a merger, sale, joint venture or collaboration, assignment, transfer, or other disposition of all or any portion of our business, assets, or stock (including in connection with any bankruptcy or similar proceedings);

who are our lawyers, auditors, and consultants;

who legal and regulatory bodies, as well as other third parties as required by law.

Telix US does not sell your Consumer Health Information or offer it in exchange for consideration without first obtaining your valid authorization to do so.

4. Exercising Your Rights

Subject to applicable exceptions, you may have certain rights regarding our processing of your Consumer Health Information under applicable law. These include the:

Right to know and confirmwhether we are collecting, sharing or selling your Consumer Health Information

Right to withdraw consentfor us to collect or share your Consumer Health Information

Right to request deletion of your Consumer Health Information

Right to correctyour Consumer Health Information

You, or your authorized agent, may exercise these rights by (1) calling us via our US Telix Hotline toll free at +1.833.214.1164 or (2) by emailing us at privacy@Telixpharma.com and providing us with your name, email address, relationship to Telix, nature of your request, and state of residence.

You must provide sufficient information to allow us to reasonably authenticate your request and verify you are the person about whom we collected the Consumer Health Information or that you are the authorized agent of such person. We may require additional information to verify and authenticate the request, which may vary depending on the Consumer Health Information we have on file for you and the nature of your request. We will be unable to respond if you do not provide sufficient detail to allow us to properly understand, evaluate, and respond to your request.

We will strive to respond to your request in a timely manner as required by law.

If you have questions regarding this Notice, or privacy concerns (including about your Consumer Health Information handling or your rights ) or complaints, please contact our Privacy Officer via privacy@telixpharma.com who will guide you on the process to follow to satisfy your request according to applicable law

Last Updated: June 1, 2026 | US-2600162

